🧠 PART 1 — BANKS ACTUALLY KI KORE

Banks never try to get 100% recall.

They use:

✔️ 1. Cost-sensitive decision

False negative (missed fraud) = very expensive
False positive (blocked card) = annoying but manageable

So they minimize:

Expected Cost=C
FN
	​

⋅FN+C
FP
	​

⋅FP

So model decision is NOT threshold 0.5 or min-prob.

It is:

fraud if P(fraud) * C_FN > (1 - P) * C_FP
✔️ 2. Probability calibration

Banks use:

Platt Scaling
Isotonic Regression

so probability = REAL probability

✔️ 3. Multi-stage system (real production)
Stage 1: fast filter (high recall)
Stage 2: ML model (XGBoost / NN)
Stage 3: rules engine + human review
Stage 4: transaction approval/block
✔️ 4. Human-in-the-loop

High risk → manual review
Not automatic accept/reject

